key_passage.text:
One of the simplest and most useful density models is the Gaussian distribution, which in one dimension (1D) is: $$\begin{aligned} p_{\theta}(x) = \frac{1}{Z}e^{-(x-\theta_1)^2/(2\theta_2)}
\end{aligned}$$ This density has two parameters $\theta_1$
and $\theta_2$, which are the mean and variance of the distribution.

